### Is it platform specific

generic

### Importance or Severity

Critical

### Description of the bug

Hi @BYGX-wcr , i encountered this failure and did some brief investigation, please help check if this only happens in our platform.

1. There is a gnmi [update](https://github.com/sonic-net/sonic-gnmi/pull/639) and it will not return the json_ietf_val if there is nothing inside the COUNTER_DB, so the test case will fail when polling from COUNTER_DB without srv6 enabled.
2. During our test, i found that the initial status of the srv6 counter(enable/disable) have an influence on the test result. On mellanox device enable leads to success and disable leads to failures, although in the test case it enable the counter before the polling. (the initial status of srv6 counter will always be disable in our setting)
3. Moreover, i found that in previous mock data test, the data polling after the insertion does not align with the mocked one, and the test case only check the number of updated response but not the content, which should have SAI_COUNTER_STAT_PACKETS=10 and SAI_COUNTER_STAT_BYTES=40960, in our platform they are both 0.

Could you please help check whether these are generic bug?

### Steps to Reproduce

we have failure in both scenarios:

1. run the test with gnmi that have the [update](https://github.com/sonic-net/sonic-gnmi/pull/639)

2. set the srv6 counter to disable before the test and run the test

### Actual Behavior and Expected Behavior

the test should not expect json_ietf_val when no data in COUNTER_DB, and return the right value injected by the mocked data

